The first two weeks have been very productive. From our first meeting, we communicated clearly that we wanted to build something tangible rather than just discuss ideas. 
We shared a few different concepts that interested us but could not immediately decide, so we agreed to meet again within a week, and each bring back an idea that we could begin to flesh out properly.
When we met again, there were several strong suggestions, and we were able to quickly decide on a direction. I contributed an idea around a language learning tool, but we ultimately chose Mei’s idea as it felt more aligned with the module criteria.
Unfortunately, I became unwell during this period and was not able to contribute as much as I would have liked to the specification stage. Despite this, the key takeaway from these two weeks is that the team is communicating very effectively. Everyone is clear on their role and understands how the project is being structured. The team continued to make solid decisions around areas such as language and storage, which I fully supported once I was feeling better.
I am now looking forward to contributing more actively in my role as a backend developer and building on the strong foundation the team has established.


